ause mortality", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42440741"}, {"study_label": "Mito agents meta (NA)", "outcome": "HF-related hospitalizations", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42440741"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ/SS-31 review (NA)", "outcome": "therapeutic effect in heart failure", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42495453"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ DCM model (preclinical)", "outcome": "diabetic myocardial injury (mtROS / TXNIP-NLRP3)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42479041"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ MI model (preclinical)", "outcome": "hemodynamic parameters (vs infarct group)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42432986"}, {"study_label": "Mito nanomedicines meta (preclinical)", "outcome": "energy metabolism in heart failure", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42022751"}, {"study_label": "Mito strategies MSK meta (preclinical)", "outcome": "disease-modifying potential (osteoporosis / OA / RA)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42727834"}, {"study_label": "Urolithin A parthenotes (preclinical)", "outcome": "preimplantation development (porcine parthenotes)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42713995"}, {"study_label": "Restorin NR animal (preclinical)", "outcome": "circulating NAD⁺ levels (vs NR chloride / NMN)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42582917"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ preeclampsia (Ph2)", "outcome": "vasodilation / placental function / pregnancy prolongation", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT07229261"}, {"study_label": "Mito-MES RCT (Ph2)", "outcome": "COVID-19 development and progression post-exposure", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT05886816"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ post-stroke (Ph2)", "outcome": "vascular health outcomes", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT06930638"}, {"study_label": "NR controlled trial (NA)", "outcome": "metabolic flexibility / exercise performance", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT07344636"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "Elamipretide", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 7, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42794697", "42229401", "40816230", "40294492", "NCT05168774", "NCT07531251", "NCT05162768"]}, {"intervention": "Nicotinamide riboside (NAD⁺ precursor)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["42009009"]}, {"intervention": "NAD⁺ supplementation (NR/NMN)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42489969"]}, {"intervention": "Idebenone", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42511474"]}, {"intervention": "Urolithin A/B", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42773997"]}, {"intervention": "PMD trial landscape (multi-agent)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42361626"]}, {"intervention": "Idebenone", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42535808"]}, {"intervention": "rAAV2/2-ND4 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42131170"]}, {"intervention": "AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42709484"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42479041", "42432986"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ and SS-31 (mito-antioxidants)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42495453"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondrial-targeted agents (unspecified)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42440741"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted nanomedicines", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42022751"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "preeclampsia", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT07229261"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ + ischemic conditioning", "disease": "post-stroke", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06930638"]}, {"intervention": "Mito-MES (Mitoquinol Mesylate)", "disease": "COVID-19", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT05886816"]}, {"intervention": "Urolithin A", "disease": "preimplantation embryo development", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42713995"]}, {"intervention": "Restorin NR (NR fumarate)", "disease": "age-related disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42582917"]}, {"intervention": "Mito-targeted strategies (multi-class)", "disease": "musculoskeletal diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42727834"]}, {"intervention": "Nicotinamide riboside", "disease": "unclear (metabolic/exercise)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07344636"]}], "insights": ["Elamipretide is the most clinically advanced mito-therapy: a Ph4 meta-analysis supports accelerated FDA approval for muscle-strength improvement in Barth syndrome (≥30 kg), yet cardiac disease modification remains explicitly unconfirmed. Two ongoing elamipretide RCTs (Ph3, Ph4) have no posted results, so the only RCT-level PMD efficacy datum in this dataset is a Ph2 NR trial showing peak VO₂ benefit only in combination with exercise (42794697, NCT07531251, NCT05162768, 42009009).", "A 2026 meta-analysis of heterogeneous mitochondria-targeted agents in chronic heart failure reported statistically significant improvements in LVEF (SMD 0.42, 95 % CI 0.31–0.53), NYHA class (RR 2.38), all-cause mortality (RR 0.62), and HF hospitalizations (RR 0.60) versus control groups. However, no extracted record includes a GDMT comparator arm, so superiority over guideline-directed medical therapy cannot be confirmed; the evidence is low confidence due to indirectness (mixed agent classes) and likely small underlying trials (42440741, 42495453).", "For LHON, the current standard of care (idebenone) shows only partial visual recovery without a statistically significant improvement in the meta-analysis, whereas rAAV2/2-ND4 gene therapy (Ph3 meta, n=175) significantly improved BCVA but did not increase responder rates. A second gene-therapy construct (AAV2-ND6 allotopic) remains entirely preclinical (mouse model). No head-to-head trial of gene therapy versus idebenone is represented in the dataset (42535808, 42131170, 42709484).", "Critical evidence gap: zero extracted records report a standard-of-care comparator arm with quantified outcomes. All 33 direction markers are mito-side only. For PMD the SOC is supportive care (no approved disease-modifying therapy), for LHON it is idebenone, and for CHF it is GDMT—yet none of these reference arms appear with effect estimates, making a true head-to-head comparison impossible from this dataset (42361626, 42440741, 42535808).", "Several well-designed late-stage PMD trials have yielded negative or inconclusive outcomes, as explicitly stated in the 2026 landscape review of 159 registered studies. MitoQ evidence in CHF is entirely preclinical (mouse MI and diabetic cardiomyopathy models showing hemodynamic and oxidative-stress benefits), and all five active NCT entries for non-PMD indications (preeclampsia, post-stroke, COVID-19, metabolic flexibility) lack posted results (42361626, 42432986, 42479041, NCT07229261, NCT06930638, NCT05886816, NCT07344636).", "The pipeline is broadening beyond the three SOC-mapped diseases into musculoskeletal disorders, preeclampsia, stroke, and metabolic/exercise physiology, but every new-indication record is either preclinical, observational, or an unreported RCT. No meta-analytic or RCT-level evidence of benefit exists yet for any non-PMD/non-LHON/non-CHF indication (42727834, 42713995, 42582917, NCT07229261, NCT05886816, NCT06930638, NCT07344636)."]}